    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Ocean Machine: Biomech is the first proper solo album from Devin Townsend, initially released in 1997 under the name Ocean Machine and later known as Ocean Machine: Biomech. Issued on Townsend’s own HevyDevy Records, it marks a major stylistic shift from his work in Strapping Young Lad, favoring expansive songwriting, atmospheric textures, and a more melodic, emotionally direct approach.\n\nMusically, the album blends progressive metal, hard rock, alternative metal, and art rock into a long-form, dynamic sequence that moves from muscular riffs to dreamy, spacious passages. Its reputation has grown steadily over time, with many listeners and critics regarding it as one of Townsend’s defining early statements for its ambition, balance of heaviness and beauty, and unusually cohesive flow.",
